                        "entry_id": "7565be9d-c3e6-3111-9974-da69592a6058",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A measure of land equal to 57,600 square feet or 1.3225 acres, formerly used in India."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "67eef962-2ffd-4770-bfcf-b53890b413a1",
                                "sense_id": "da7b8cf0-06fb-3b35-b3c9-6bb7e22fefcf",
                                "text": "This fort of mud was formerly built by the Curumbas, covering forty cawnies of ground with two boundary walls, and was long ruled by them."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ec9c6266-2675-4152-9b4a-b8e0d4320d50",
                                "sense_id": "da7b8cf0-06fb-3b35-b3c9-6bb7e22fefcf",
                                "text": "If we take the best cotton land, paying a land tax of Rupees 3-5-5 per cawnie, the proportion would be upwards of 33 per cent."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "302f59fa-7b15-4cc6-84cc-b3ac05e903dc",
                                "sense_id": "da7b8cf0-06fb-3b35-b3c9-6bb7e22fefcf",
                                "text": "We shall now consider the cost of cultivating one cawnie of dry Poonjay land with Indigo by the native cultivator who does not irrigate."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1959eea8-bdef-4939-9cb3-2137e0c43b26",
                                "sense_id": "da7b8cf0-06fb-3b35-b3c9-6bb7e22fefcf",
                                "text": "On the Nilgiris, the cawnie was initially utilised exclusively in measuring settler occupation."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
